 },
 "body": [
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "1"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 1"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.1",
      "label": "DCS 1.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "yasyonmeṣanimeṣābhyāṃ jagataḥ pralayodayau",
       "translated_text": "We praise that <s>Śaṃkara</s>, by whose opening and closing of the eyes there are the dissolution and arising of the world,",
       "segment_number": 48970
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "taṃ śakticakravibhavaprabhavaṃ śaṃkaraṃ stumaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "the source of the glory of the circle of powers.",
       "segment_number": 48971
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.2",
      "label": "DCS 1.2"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "yatra sthitamidaṃ sarvaṃ kāryaṃ yasmāc ca nirgatam",
       "translated_text": "In whom all this effect stands, and from whom it has issued forth,",
       "segment_number": 48972
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tasyānāvṛtarūpatvān na nirodho'sti kutracit ||",
       "translated_text": "because his form is unobscured, there is no obstruction anywhere.",
       "segment_number": 48973
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.3",
      "label": "DCS 1.3"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "jāgradādivibhede'pi tadabhinne prasarpati",
       "translated_text": "Even amid the distinctions beginning with waking, it spreads forth as non-different from that;",
       "segment_number": 48974
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "nivartate nijān naiva svabhāvādupalabdhṛtaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "the perceiver never withdraws from his own intrinsic nature.",
       "segment_number": 48975
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.4",
      "label": "DCS 1.4"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "ahaṃ sukhī ca duḥkhī ca raktaścetyādisaṃvidaḥ",
       "translated_text": "The cognitions 'I am happy,' 'I am unhappy,' 'I am attached,' and so on",
       "segment_number": 48976
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "sukhādyavasthānusyūte vartante 'nyatra tāḥ sphuṭam ||",
       "translated_text": "clearly occur elsewhere, threaded upon the states such as pleasure.",
       "segment_number": 48977
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.5",
      "label": "DCS 1.5"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "na duḥkhaṃ na sukhaṃ yatra na grāhyaṃ grāhakaṃ na ca",
       "translated_text": "Where there is neither pain nor pleasure, neither object grasped nor grasper,",
       "segment_number": 48978
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "na cāsti mūḍhabhāvo'pi tadasti paramārthataḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "and not even a state of dullness, that exists in the highest reality.",
       "segment_number": 48979
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.6",
      "label": "DCS 1.6"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "yataḥ karaṇavargo 'yaṃ vimūḍho 'mūḍhavat svayam",
       "translated_text": "Because this group of instruments, itself bewildered, as if unbewildered,",
       "segment_number": 48980
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "sahāntareṇa cakreṇa pravṛttisthitisaṃhṛtīḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "attains activity, maintenance, and withdrawal together with the inner wheel.",
       "segment_number": 48981
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.7",
      "label": "DCS 1.7"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "labhate tatprayatnena parīkṣyaṃ tattvamādarāt",
       "translated_text": "Therefore that principle is to be examined with effort and respect,",
       "segment_number": 48982
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "yataḥ svatantratā tasya sarvatreyam akṛtrimā ||",
       "translated_text": "because its autonomy is everywhere natural and uncontrived.",
       "segment_number": 48983
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.8",
      "label": "DCS 1.8"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "na hīcchānodanasyāyaṃ prerakatvena vartate",
       "translated_text": "For this does not function as the impeller of one who is driven by desire;",
       "segment_number": 48984
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "api tv ātmabalasparśāt puruṣas tatsamo bhavet ||",
       "translated_text": "rather, through contact with the power of the self, the person becomes equal to it.",
       "segment_number": 48985
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.9",
      "label": "DCS 1.9"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "nijāśuddhyāsamarthasya kartavyeṣvabhilāṣiṇaḥ",
       "translated_text": "For one who is incapable because of his own impurity, yet desirous of action,",
       "segment_number": 48986
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "yadā kṣobhaḥ pralīyeta tadā syātparamaṃ padam ||",
       "translated_text": "when agitation dissolves, then the supreme state comes to be.",
       "segment_number": 48987
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.10",
      "label": "DCS 1.10"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tadāsyākṛtrimo dharmo jñatvakartṛtvalakṣaṇaḥ",
       "translated_text": "Then his uncontrived nature, marked by knowing and agency, appears,",
       "segment_number": 48988
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "yatas tadepsitaṃ sarvaṃ jānāti ca karoti ca ||",
       "translated_text": "because then he knows and does everything that he desires.",
       "segment_number": 48989
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.11",
      "label": "DCS 1.11"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tamadhiṣṭhātṛbhāvena svabhāvamavalokayan",
       "translated_text": "Seeing that intrinsic nature as the presiding ruler,",
       "segment_number": 48990
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "smayamāna ivāste yas tasyeyaṃ kusṛtiḥ kutaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "one who remains as if smiling: how could this bad course belong to him?",
       "segment_number": 48991
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.12",
      "label": "DCS 1.12"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "nābhāvo bhāvyatāmeti na ca tatrāsty amūḍhatā",
       "translated_text": "Non-existence does not become an object to be contemplated, nor is there undeludedness there,",
       "segment_number": 48992
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "yato 'bhiyogasaṃsparśāt tadāsīd iti niścayaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "because from contact with application there is the certainty, 'that existed then.'",
       "segment_number": 48993
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.13",
      "label": "DCS 1.13"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "atas tat kṛtrimaṃ jñeyaṃ sauṣuptapadavat sadā",
       "translated_text": "Therefore that should always be known as artificial, like the state of deep sleep,",
       "segment_number": 48994
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "na tv evaṃ smaryamāṇatvaṃ tat tattvaṃ pratipadyate ||",
       "translated_text": "but that reality is not reached merely by being remembered in this way.",
       "segment_number": 48995
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.14",
      "label": "DCS 1.14"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "avasthāyugalaṃ cātra kāryakartṛtvaśabditam",
       "translated_text": "Here the pair of states is called being-effect and being-agent;",
       "segment_number": 48996
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "kāryatā kṣayiṇī tatra kartṛtvaṃ punarakṣayam ||",
       "translated_text": "being an effect is perishable there, but agency is imperishable.",
       "segment_number": 48997
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.15",
      "label": "DCS 1.15"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "kāryonmukhaḥ prayatno yaḥ kevalaṃ so 'tra lupyate",
       "translated_text": "The effort that is directed toward an effect alone is what disappears here;",
       "segment_number": 48998
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tasmiṃl lupte vilupto 'smītyabudhaḥ pratipadyate ||",
       "translated_text": "when that has disappeared, the ignorant person concludes, 'I have disappeared.'",
       "segment_number": 48999
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.16",
      "label": "DCS 1.16"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "na tu yo 'ntarmukho bhāvaḥ sarvajñatvaguṇāspadam",
       "translated_text": "But the inward-turned state, the locus of the quality of omniscience,",
       "segment_number": 49000
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tasya lopaḥ kadācitsyād anyasyānupalambhanāt ||",
       "translated_text": "can never disappear, because nothing else is apprehended.",
       "segment_number": 49001
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.17",
      "label": "DCS 1.17"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tasyopalabdhiḥ satataṃ tripadāvyabhicāriṇī",
       "translated_text": "The apprehension of it is constant, never deviating from the three states,",
       "segment_number": 49002
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "nityaṃ syāt suprabuddhasya tadādyante parasya tu ||",
       "translated_text": "and is always present for the well-awakened; for another it is only at their beginning and end.",
       "segment_number": 49003
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.18",
      "label": "DCS 1.18"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "jñānajñeyasvarūpiṇyā śaktyā paramayā yutaḥ",
       "translated_text": "Joined with the supreme power whose nature is knowledge and the knowable,",
       "segment_number": 49004
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "padadvaye vibhurbhāti tadanyatra tu cinmayaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "the all-pervading one shines in the two states; elsewhere, however, he is consciousness itself.",
       "segment_number": 49005
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.19",
      "label": "DCS 1.19"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "guṇādispandaniḥṣyandāḥ sāmānyaspandasaṃśrayāt",
       "translated_text": "The outflows of <s>spanda</s> beginning with the qualities, because they rest upon the general <s>spanda</s>,",
       "segment_number": 49006
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "labdhātmalābhāḥ satataṃ syur jñasyāparipanthinaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "having obtained their own existence, are always no hindrance to the knower.",
       "segment_number": 49007
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.20",
      "label": "DCS 1.20"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "aprabuddhadhiyas tv ete svasthitisthaganodyatāḥ",
       "translated_text": "But for those whose intellect is unawakened, these, intent on covering their own state,",
       "segment_number": 49008
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "pātayanti duruttāre ghore saṃsāravartmani ||",
       "translated_text": "cast them down onto the terrible path of <s>saṃsāra</s>, hard to cross.",
       "segment_number": 49009
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.21",
      "label": "DCS 1.21"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "ataḥ satatam udyuktaḥ spandatattvaviviktaye",
       "translated_text": "Therefore, one who is constantly intent on discerning the principle of <s>spanda</s>",
       "segment_number": 49010
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "jāgradeva nijaṃ bhāvam acireṇādhigacchati ||",
       "translated_text": "quickly attains his own state even while awake.",
       "segment_number": 49011
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.22",
      "label": "DCS 1.22"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "atikruddhaḥ prahṛṣṭo vā kiṃ karomīti vā mṛśan",
       "translated_text": "When someone is extremely angry, or overjoyed, or reflecting, 'What shall I do?',",
       "segment_number": 49012
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "dhāvanvā yatpadaṃ gacchet tatra spandaḥ pratiṣṭhitaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "or running, whatever state he reaches, <s>spanda</s> is established there.",
       "segment_number": 49013
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.23",
      "label": "DCS 1.23"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "yāmavasthāṃ samālambya yadayaṃ mama vakṣyati",
       "translated_text": "Taking hold of the state from which 'this will speak to me,'",
       "segment_number": 49014
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tadavaśyaṃ kariṣye 'hamiti saṃkalpya tiṣṭhati ||",
       "translated_text": "he remains resolved, 'I shall certainly do that.'",
       "segment_number": 49015
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.24",
      "label": "DCS 1.24"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tāmāśrityordhvamārgeṇa candrasūryāv ubhāv api",
       "translated_text": "Relying on that, by the upward path, both moon and sun",
       "segment_number": 49016
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "sauṣumne'dhvany astamito hitvā brahmāṇḍagocaram ||",
       "translated_text": "set along the <s>suṣumnā</s> path, abandoning the sphere of the cosmic egg.",
       "segment_number": 49017
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_1.25",
      "label": "DCS 1.25"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tadā tasminmahāvyomni pralīnaśaśibhāskare",
       "translated_text": "Then, in that great ether, when moon and sun have dissolved,",
       "segment_number": 49018
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "sauṣuptapadavan mūḍhaḥ prabuddhaḥ syād anāvṛtaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "the dull person is as in the state of deep sleep, but the awakened one is unobscured.",
       "segment_number": 49019
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "2"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 2"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_2.1",
      "label": "DCS 2.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tadākramya balaṃ mantrāḥ sarvajñabalaśālinaḥ",
       "translated_text": "Having entered into that power, mantras, endowed with the power of omniscience,",
       "segment_number": 49020
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "pravartante'dhikārāya karaṇānīva dehinām ||",
       "translated_text": "proceed to their office, like the instruments of embodied beings.",
       "segment_number": 49021
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_2.2",
      "label": "DCS 2.2"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tatraiva sampralīyante śāntarūpā nirañjanāḥ",
       "translated_text": "There itself they completely dissolve, peaceful in form and stainless,",
       "segment_number": 49022
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "sahārādhakacittena tenaite śivadharmiṇaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "together with the mind of the worshiper; therefore these have the nature of <s>Śiva</s>.",
       "segment_number": 49023
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_2.3",
      "label": "DCS 2.3"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "yasmātsarvamayo jīvaḥ sarvabhāvasamudbhavāt",
       "translated_text": "Because the individual soul is made of all, since all states arise from it,",
       "segment_number": 49024
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tatsaṃvedanarūpeṇa tādātmyapratipattitaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "through the form of its awareness there is the realization of identity with them.",
       "segment_number": 49025
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_2.4",
      "label": "DCS 2.4"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tasmācchabdārthacintāsu na sāvasthā na yā śivaḥ",
       "translated_text": "Therefore, in thoughts about word and meaning, there is no state that is not <s>Śiva</s>,",
       "segment_number": 49026
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "bhoktaiva bhogyabhāvena sadā sarvatra saṃsthitaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "for the enjoyer himself, in the form of the enjoyed, is always established everywhere.",
       "segment_number": 49027
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_2.5",
      "label": "DCS 2.5"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "iti vā yasya saṃvittiḥ krīḍātvenākhilaṃ jagat",
       "translated_text": "Thus, for one whose awareness is that the entire world is play,",
       "segment_number": 49028
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "sa paśyansatataṃ yukto jīvanmukto na saṃśayaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "he, seeing constantly and yoked, is liberated while living; there is no doubt.",
       "segment_number": 49029
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_2.6",
      "label": "DCS 2.6"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "ayamevodayastasya dhyeyasya dhyāyicetasi",
       "translated_text": "This very arising of that object of meditation in the mind of the meditator",
       "segment_number": 49030
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tadātmatāsamāpattir icchataḥ sādhakasya yā ||",
       "translated_text": "is the attainment of identity with it for the practitioner who desires it.",
       "segment_number": 49031
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_2.7",
      "label": "DCS 2.7"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "yamevāmṛtaprāptir ayam evātmano grahaḥ",
       "translated_text": "This alone is the attainment of immortality; this alone is the grasping of the self;",
       "segment_number": 49032
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "iyaṃ nirvāṇadīkṣā ca śivasadbhāvadāyinī ||",
       "translated_text": "and this is the initiation into <s>nirvāṇa</s>, bestowing the true state of <s>Śiva</s>.",
       "segment_number": 49033
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "3"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 3"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.1",
      "label": "DCS 3.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "yathecchābhyarthito dhātā jāgrato 'rthān hṛdi sthitān",
       "translated_text": "Just as the creator, entreated according to one's wish, for a waking embodied being",
       "segment_number": 49034
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "somasūryodayaṃ kṛtvā sampādayati dehinaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "brings about the desired objects resting in the heart by producing the rise of moon and sun,",
       "segment_number": 49035
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.2",
      "label": "DCS 3.2"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tathā svapne 'pyabhīṣṭārthān praṇayasyānatikramāt",
       "translated_text": "so too in dream, because he does not transgress affection,",
       "segment_number": 49036
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "nityaṃ sphuṭataraṃ madhye sthito'vaśyaṃ prakāśayet ||",
       "translated_text": "standing always in the middle, he must manifest desired objects even more clearly.",
       "segment_number": 49037
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.3",
      "label": "DCS 3.3"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "anyathā tu svatantrā syāt sṛṣṭis taddharmakatvataḥ",
       "translated_text": "Otherwise creation would be independent, since it has that as its nature,",
       "segment_number": 49038
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "satataṃ laukikasyeva jāgratsvapnapadadvaye ||",
       "translated_text": "always, as for an ordinary person, in the two states of waking and dream.",
       "segment_number": 49039
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.4",
      "label": "DCS 3.4"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "yathā hy artho 'sphuṭo dṛṣṭaḥ sāvadhāne'pi cetasi",
       "translated_text": "For just as an object seen indistinctly, even in an attentive mind,",
       "segment_number": 49040
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "bhūyaḥ sphuṭataro bhāti svabalodyogabhāvitaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "appears again more clearly when made manifest by the exertion of its own power,",
       "segment_number": 49041
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.5",
      "label": "DCS 3.5"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tathā yatparamārthena yena yatra yathā sthitam",
       "translated_text": "so whatever is established in the highest reality, by whatever means, wherever, and however,",
       "segment_number": 49042
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tattathā balamākramya na cirāt sampravartate ||",
       "translated_text": "that, having entered into that power in that very way, comes into operation before long.",
       "segment_number": 49043
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.6",
      "label": "DCS 3.6"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "durbalo'pi tadākramya yataḥ kārye pravartate",
       "translated_text": "For even one who is weak, having entered into that, proceeds in action.",
       "segment_number": 49044
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "ācchādayedbubhukṣāṃ ca tathā yo 'tibubhukṣitaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "And one who is very hungry should conceal even his hunger and desire for food.",
       "segment_number": 49045
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.7",
      "label": "DCS 3.7"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "anenādhiṣṭhite dehe yathā sarvajñatādayaḥ",
       "translated_text": "Just as, when this body is presided over by that principle, omniscience and the other powers arise,",
       "segment_number": 49046
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tathā svātmanyadhiṣṭhānāt sarvatraivaṃ bhaviṣyati ||",
       "translated_text": "so, through its being established in one's own self, this will come to be everywhere.",
       "segment_number": 49047
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.8",
      "label": "DCS 3.8"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "glānir viluṇṭhikā dehe tasyāścājñānataḥ sṛtiḥ",
       "translated_text": "Weakness is a plunderer in the body, and its movement comes from ignorance.",
       "segment_number": 49048
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tadunmeṣaviluptaṃ cet kutaḥ sā syādahetukā ||",
       "translated_text": "If it is destroyed by that opening of awareness, how could that causeless weakness exist?",
       "segment_number": 49049
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.9",
      "label": "DCS 3.9"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "ekacintāprasaktasya yataḥ syād aparodayaḥ",
       "translated_text": "When one is absorbed in a single thought, and another arising may occur from it,",
       "segment_number": 49050
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "unmeṣaḥ sa tu vijñeyaḥ svayaṃ tamupalakṣayet ||",
       "translated_text": "that should be understood as <s>unmeṣa</s> (the opening of awareness); one should perceive it for oneself.",
       "segment_number": 49051
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.10",
      "label": "DCS 3.10"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "ato bindur ato nādo rūpam asmād ato rasaḥ",
       "translated_text": "From this come the point, from this the sound, from this form, and from this taste;",
       "segment_number": 49052
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "pravartante 'cireṇaiva kṣobhakatvena dehinaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "for the embodied being they quickly begin to operate as agitating forces.",
       "segment_number": 49053
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.11",
      "label": "DCS 3.11"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "didṛkṣayeva sarvārthān yadā vyāpyāvatiṣṭhate",
       "translated_text": "When, as if from a desire to see all objects, it remains after pervading them,",
       "segment_number": 49054
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tadā kiṃ bahunoktena svayam evāvabhotsyate ||",
       "translated_text": "then, what need is there of saying much? It will be understood by itself.",
       "segment_number": 49055
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.12",
      "label": "DCS 3.12"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "prabuddhaḥ sarvadā tiṣṭhejjñānenālokya gocaram",
       "translated_text": "One should remain always awakened, viewing the field of experience through knowledge.",
       "segment_number": 49056
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "ekatrāropayetsarvaṃ tato 'nyena na pīḍyate ||",
       "translated_text": "One should place everything upon one point; then one is not afflicted by anything else.",
       "segment_number": 49057
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.13",
      "label": "DCS 3.13"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "śabdarāśisamutthasya śaktivargasya bhogyatām",
       "translated_text": "The host of powers arising from the mass of speech becomes an object of enjoyment.",
       "segment_number": 49058
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "kalāviluptavibhavo gataḥ sansa paśuḥ smṛtaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "One whose glory has been obliterated by the <s>kalā</s>s has gone to that state and is remembered as a <s>paśu</s> (bound soul).",
       "segment_number": 49059
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.14",
      "label": "DCS 3.14"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "parāmṛtarasāpāyas tasya yaḥ pratyayodbhavaḥ",
       "translated_text": "For him there is a loss of the taste of the supreme nectar, which is produced by cognition;",
       "segment_number": 49060
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tenāsvatantratāmeti sa ca tanmātragocaraḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "through that he falls into dependence, and that cognition has only the subtle elements as its field.",
       "segment_number": 49061
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.15",
      "label": "DCS 3.15"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "svarūpāvaraṇe cāsya śaktayaḥ satatotthitāḥ",
       "translated_text": "And when his own nature is covered, the powers are constantly arising,",
       "segment_number": 49062
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "yataḥ śabdānuvedhena na vinā pratyayodbhavaḥ ||",
       "translated_text": "because the arising of cognition does not occur without being pierced by sound.",
       "segment_number": 49063
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.16",
      "label": "DCS 3.16"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "seyaṃ kriyātmikā śaktiḥ śivasya paśuvartinī",
       "translated_text": "This is the action-natured <s>śakti</s> of <s>Śiva</s>, operating in the bound being.",
       "segment_number": 49064
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "bandhayitrī svamārgasthā jñātā siddhyupapādikā ||",
       "translated_text": "Standing on its own path, it binds; when known, it brings about accomplishment.",
       "segment_number": 49065
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.17",
      "label": "DCS 3.17"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "tanmātrodayarūpeṇa mano'hambuddhivartinā",
       "translated_text": "By the form of the arising of the subtle elements, operating in mind, ego, and intellect,",
       "segment_number": 49066
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "puryaṣṭakena saṃruddhas tadutthaṃ pratyayodbhavam ||",
       "translated_text": "he is confined by the eightfold city and by the cognition that arises from it.",
       "segment_number": 49067
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.18",
      "label": "DCS 3.18"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "bhuṅkte paravaśo bhogaṃ tadbhāvātsaṃsaredataḥ",
       "translated_text": "Powerless, he experiences enjoyment born from that condition; therefore he transmigrates.",
       "segment_number": 49068
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "saṃsṛtipralayasyāsya kāraṇaṃ sampracakṣmahe ||",
       "translated_text": "Now we shall explain the cause of this cycle of transmigration and dissolution.",
       "segment_number": 49069
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_3.19",
      "label": "DCS 3.19"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "yadā tv ekatra saṃrūḍhas tadā tasya layodayau",
       "translated_text": "But when he is firmly rooted in the one place, then, controlling its dissolution and arising,",
       "segment_number": 49070
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "niyacchan bhoktṛtām eti tataś cakreśvaro bhavet ||",
       "translated_text": "he attains the state of enjoyer; thereafter he becomes the lord of the wheel.",
       "segment_number": 49071
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "attributes": {
    "type": "chapter",
    "n": "4"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "tag": "head",
     "attributes": {},
     "text": "Chapter 4"
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_4.1",
      "label": "DCS 4.1"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "agādhasaṃśayāmbhodhisamuttaraṇatāriṇīm",
       "translated_text": "I bow to that wondrous speech of the guru, whose words have manifold meanings,",
       "segment_number": 49072
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "vande vicitrārthapadāṃ citrāṃ tāṃ gurubhāratīm ||",
       "translated_text": "a ferryboat for crossing the unfathomable ocean of doubt.",
       "segment_number": 49073
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tag": "lg",
     "attributes": {
      "id": "DCS_4.2",
      "label": "DCS 4.2"
     },
     "children": [
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "labdhvāpyalabhyam etajjñānadhanaṃ hṛdguhāntakṛtanihiteḥ",
       "translated_text": "Having obtained this treasure of knowledge, hard to obtain, deposited within the cave of the heart,",
       "segment_number": 49074
      },
      {
       "tag": "l",
       "attributes": {},
       "text": "vasuguptavacchivāya hi bhavati sadā sarvalokasya ||",
       "translated_text": "like <s>Vasugupta</s>, one is always for <s>Śiva</s>, for the sake of the whole world.",
       "segment_number": 49075
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
